#subtitle: Setting the party's ideological direction.

= Questions of Ideology

The S&D is torn between many different ideological currents. Who shall we favor for now?

[? if ideology != 0 : We have previously chosen a [+ ideology +] ideology. Changing it will have consequences. ?]

- @radical_republican: We will bring a revolution without revolution, and to make decisions quickly without infighting.
- @new_democrat: Just as the democrats before us, we too shall encourage economic democracy across Europa.
- @robin_hoods: The rich shall be heavily taxed to destroy their hegemony, to build an egalitarian social republic.
- @mixed: Only a mixed economy can bring about the benefits of both capitalism and socialism without their flaws.
- @blue_labour: While we should remain economcially left wing, society needs a moral upbringing to bring a harmonious society.
- @easy_discard

@radical_republican
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "girondins") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "girondins"; girondins_strength += 10; communist_coalition += 1; girondins_dissent -= 5; epp_relation -= 3; renew_relation -= 5; nationalization_support += 1; left_relation += 5

The radical left from the latin parties supports groundbreaking change, and a reconcilliation with the Left. Our party will slowly evolve into a centralist party.

@new_democrat
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "neodemocrat") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "neodemocrat"; neodemocrat_strength += 10; neodemocrat_dissent -= 10; girondins_dissent -= 5; epp_relation += 2; green_relations += 2; redistributor_dissent -= 1; regulationist_dissent +=5; leftcons_dissent -= 5

The Neodemocrats, supported by the nordic parties, wishes to finally bring economic democracy onto the mainstream. Our party will slowly evolve into a bloc party.

@robin_hoods
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "redistributor") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "redistributor"; redistributor_strength += 10; wtb_support += 1; redistributor_dissent -= 5; left_relation -= 3; green_relation += 3

The redistributors mostly consist of central european parties that wish to enact confiscatory taxation to fund more social services. Our party will slowly evolve into a people's party.

@mixed
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "regulationist") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "regulationist"; regulationist_strength += 10; wtb_support += 1; regulationist_dissent -= 5; left_relation -= 5; green_relation += 8; renew_relation +=8

The regulationists of Ruthenia, Greece, and Novgorod wish to regulate the economy so people can live their lives without much interference. Our party will slowly evolve into a confederal party.

@blue_labour
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "leftcons") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "leftcons"; leftcons_strength += 10; democratization += 1; leftcons_dissent -= 5; epp_relation += 8; renew_relation += 5; left_relation -= 8; green_relation -= 3; moderate_plan_support += 1

The left-conservatives in Turkiye and "Eastern Europe" prefer a syncretic style of governance, bringing a left wing economy along with a right wing society. Our party will slowly evolve into a syncretic party.


@changed
on-arrival: left_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5

We have changed ideologies. Many in the party feel unmoored.
